{
  "duration": 68.54,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 0.259,
      "text": "So"
    },
    {
      "start": 0.56,
      "end": 1.319,
      "text": "welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.879,
      "end": 3.519,
      "text": "It's time to solve one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.099,
      "end": 4.779,
      "text": "Now in this problem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.359,
      "end": 6.42,
      "text": "a 13-meter ladder"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.839,
      "end": 7.719,
      "text": "is touching a window"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.22,
      "end": 9.739,
      "text": "which is 12 meter above the ground."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.359,
      "end": 13.899,
      "text": "The question is asking us to find how far the foot of the ladder"
    },
    {
      "start": 14.319,
      "end": 15.0,
      "text": "is from the wall."
    },
    {
      "start": 15.699,
      "end": 15.899,
      "text": "Here,"
    },
    {
      "start": 16.26,
      "end": 16.719,
      "text": "the ladder,"
    },
    {
      "start": 17.26,
      "end": 17.659,
      "text": "the wall,"
    },
    {
      "start": 18.059,
      "end": 18.639,
      "text": "and the ground"
    },
    {
      "start": 19.1,
      "end": 21.02,
      "text": "make a right-angled triangle."
    },
    {
      "start": 21.619,
      "end": 25.319,
      "text": "The ladder will be the hypotenuse because it is the slant side."
    },
    {
      "start": 25.84,
      "end": 27.499,
      "text": "The wall height is the perpendicular,"
    },
    {
      "start": 28.039,
      "end": 29.359,
      "text": "and the distance from the wall"
    },
    {
      "start": 29.779,
      "end": 32.159,
      "text": "to the foot of the ladder is the base."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.919,
      "end": 34.139,
      "text": "Let the base be x meter."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.619,
      "end": 40.339,
      "text": "Using Pythagoras Theorem, hypotenuse square is equal to base square plus perpendicular square."
    },
    {
      "start": 40.899,
      "end": 45.479,
      "text": "So we can write 13 square is equal to x square plus 12 square."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.899,
      "end": 46.979,
      "text": "That means"
    },
    {
      "start": 47.279,
      "end": 51.099,
      "text": "169 is equal to x square plus 144."
    },
    {
      "start": 51.5,
      "end": 58.759,
      "text": "So x square is equal to 169 minus 144. After subtracting, x square is equal to 25."
    },
    {
      "start": 59.139,
      "end": 61.52,
      "text": "So x is equal to root 25,"
    },
    {
      "start": 61.859,
      "end": 62.519,
      "text": "which is five."
    },
    {
      "start": 63.439,
      "end": 65.979,
      "text": "Hence, the foot of the ladder is five meters from the wall."
    },
    {
      "start": 66.58,
      "end": 68.54,
      "text": "So the correct option is option C."
    }
  ],
